247
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:26,400
At current prices, crude represents

248
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:29,360
roughly 60% of what you are paying at

249
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:31,400
the pump. That is about $1.86 out of

250
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:32,840
every $3.11

251
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:35,400
that goes straight to the oil market

252
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:38,240
before anyone even touches it. Refining

253
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:41,200
and processing adds about 9%, roughly

254
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:43,560
$0.28 a gallon. Then come the taxes. The

255
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:45,520
federal government charges a flat 18.4

256
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:47,800
cents per gallon on gasoline, no matter

257
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:50,200
what the price is. On top of that, every

258
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:52,720
