267
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:11,680
government, not to the station owner.

268
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:14,960
Distribution and freight adds another

269
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:16,720
11%, roughly 34 cents per gallon, to

270
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:18,920
cover the pipelines, terminals, and

271
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:21,240
truck deliveries. Then come credit card

272
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:24,080
fees. Every time a customer swipes a

273
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:26,080
card, and about 85% of fuel purchases

274
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:27,600
are made with plastic, the payment

275
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:29,520
network charges the station owner a

276
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:34,360
percentage of the gross sale, typically

277
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:36,440
between 1.5 and 3 and 1/2%. At $3.11 per

278
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:38,640
gallon, that works out to about 8 cents

279
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:40,480
per gallon going straight to Visa or

280
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:43,280
MasterCard or the bank that issued the

281
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:45,120
card. Add all that up and what is left?

282
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:47,400
What the station actually keeps before

283
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:49,560
paying any of its own operating costs

284
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:51,480
averages around 30 to 35 cents per

285
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:53,240
gallon in gross margin. According to

286
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:55,960
data from the Oil Price Information

287
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:57,920
Service published in January of 2025,

288
00:09:55,960 --> 00:10:01,280
the national average fuel gross margin

289
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:03,040
was 35.7 cents per gallon. And after

290
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:04,920
paying for labor, electricity,

291
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:07,280
maintenance, and everything else, the

292
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:09,800
net profit on fuel is closer to 10 to 15

293
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:12,360
cents per gallon. Sell 100,000 gallons a

294
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:14,520
month and you make 10,000 to 15,000

295
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:16,880
dollars in net fuel profit, before the

296
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:19,120
loan payment, before property taxes,

297
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,600
before anything. Meanwhile, the bank

298
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:22,920
that issued the card the customer used

299
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:25,040
by that fuel earns more per gallon in

300
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:26,840
swipe fees than the station owner earns

301
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,880
in actual profit.

302
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:30,720
That is not an exaggeration. It is the

303
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:32,120
math. There is a reason gas station

304
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:33,960
owners are obsessed with what their

305
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:35,760
competitors charge. Research

306
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:38,280
consistently shows that a difference of

307
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:40,080
as little as 3 to 5 cents per gallon is

308
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:41,640
enough to divert the majority of price

309
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:44,280
sensitive drivers to a competing

310
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:46,320
station. Fuel is one of the most price

311
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:47,760
transparent products in retail. You can

312
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:50,040
read the competitor's price from your

313
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:52,320
car 2 seconds before you decide whether

314
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:54,200
to turn in. So, when one station drops

315
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:56,640
its price to pull traffic, the stations

316
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:59,040
nearby have to respond. Margins shrink

317
00:10:56,640 --> 00:11:00,720
across the whole corridor. Nobody wants

318
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:03,160
to be the station charging more, so

319
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:05,360
everybody charges less. This dynamic,

320
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:06,920
called a price war, is common in markets

321
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,960
where two or three stations sit within

322
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:10,640
half a mile of each other. Economists

323
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:12,320
have documented an interesting pattern

324
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:14,760
in fuel pricing called rockets and

325
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:17,280
feathers. When wholesale prices go up,

326
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:18,880
retail prices rise fast, like a rocket.

327
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,720
When wholesale prices fall, retail

328
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:22,600
prices drop slowly, like a feather

329
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:24,520
drifting down. Station owners push

330
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:26,240
prices up immediately when costs rise

331
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:28,480
because they cannot afford to absorb the

332
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:30,560
loss, but they hold prices higher for

333
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:32,480
longer when costs fall because they are

334
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:34,400
trying to recoup the margins they lost

335
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:37,000
during the previous spike. This is

336
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:39,640
rational, not malicious. It is what thin

337
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,960
margin businesses do to survive. Now,

338
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:43,120
here is the part that changes

339
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:45,040
everything. Fuel gets customers to your

340
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:46,640
property. The store is where you

341
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:48,280
actually make money. According to

342
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:51,920
National Association of Convenience

343
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:53,520
Stores data, fuel sales made up 67.3%

344
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:56,040
of total convenience store revenue in

345
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:57,800
2023. But that same fuel contributed

346
00:11:56,040 --> 00:12:00,160
only 38.6%

347
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:02,920
of total gross profit. The inside store,

348
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:05,520
coffee, snacks, drinks, food, lottery

349
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:07,800
tickets, made up 35% of revenue but

350
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:10,160
generated 61.2%

351
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:12,240
of total gross profit. Think about what

352
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:14,200
that means. More than six out of every

353
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,960
$10 of profit at the average American

354
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:18,040
gas station comes from inside the

355
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:20,240
building, not from the pumps. The reason

356
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:22,960
is margins. Fuel gross margin runs

357
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:25,520
around 11%. Inside store gross margin

358
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:27,440
runs between 30 and 50% depending on the

359
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:29,640
category. A can of soda costs the

360
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:33,240
station owner roughly 40 cents and sells

361
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:35,320
for $2. That is a margin of over 75%. A

362
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:37,880
bag of chips that cost 25 cents

363
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:39,360
wholesale retails for $1.50. Cigarettes

364
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:41,600
carry thin margins because the

365
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:43,440
manufacturers control the pricing, but

366
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,120
they drive enormous foot traffic from

367
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,720
regular buyers who come in multiple

368
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:49,160
times a week. And then there is

369
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:51,800
tobacco's replacement, energy drinks,

370
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:53,680
premium coffee, and prepared food. Let

371
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:55,320
us get very specific about something. A

372
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:57,760
cup brewed coffee costs the station

373
00:12:55,320 --> 00:13:00,120
owner roughly 23 cents in beans, the

374
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:01,960
cup, and the lid. It sells for between

375
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:04,280
three and five dollars depending on size

376
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:06,960
and the market. That is a gross margin

377
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:08,920
of over 90% even after factoring in the

378
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,800
cost of the machine, electricity, and

379
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:13,200
the occasional spilled pot, the net

380
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:15,160
margin on coffee is around 40%. Now

381
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:18,000
compare that to a standard vehicle fill

382
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:19,720
up. 12 gallons of fuel at a retail price

383
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,040
of $3.11

384
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:24,360
totals $37.32

385
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:26,760
in revenue. The gross pool margin, the

386
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:29,080
station's cut before operating costs, is

387
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:31,960
about 30 cents per gallon, so roughly

388
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:33,400
$3.60 on the whole transaction. The

389
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:36,080
credit card swipe fee on that

390
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:38,280
transaction takes back about 82-cents.

391
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:40,160
Operating expenses eat more. The net to

392
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:42,600
the station owner on that entire fill-up

393
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:44,320
is somewhere around 40 to 60-cents. A

394
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:45,880
single cup of coffee generates more

395
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,960
bottom-line profit than pumping

396
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:50,040
12-gallons of gasoline. This is why

397
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:51,920
chains like Wawa, Sheetz, and Casey's

398
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,760
have spent the last two decades building

399
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:56,400
serious food programs inside their

400
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:58,120
stores. Casey's, based in Iowa, now

401
00:13:56,400 --> 00:14:00,520
operates one of the largest pizza chains

402
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:02,920
in the United States by store count

403
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:04,320
inside its gas stations. Wawa has built

404
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:06,320
a cult following around its

405
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:07,720
made-to-order hoagies. These companies

406
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:10,200
understood early that the food is the

407
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,920
business. The fuel is the advertisement.

408
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:14,000
Smart operators do not stop at the

409
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:15,680
coffee machine. The automatic car wash

410
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
is one of the highest margin additions a

411
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,720
station can make. A tunnel wash with

412
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,880
automated equipment runs with minimal

413
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:24,480
labor, and the gross profit margin

414
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:26,400
regularly exceeds 50%. Membership

415
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:28,640
programs, where customers pay a fixed

416
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:30,480
monthly fee for unlimited washes, have

417
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:32,480
transformed the economics of car wash

418
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:34,280
operations, creating predictable

419
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:36,520
recurring revenue on top of walk-in

420
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:38,400
traffic. ATM machines installed inside

421
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:40,560
the store earn the operator a commission

422
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:42,760
on every transaction, typically between

423
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:44,960
one and two dollars per withdrawal. This

424
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:46,920
requires no labor, no inventory, and

425
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:49,000
minimal maintenance. State lottery

426
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:50,920
terminals, in states where convenience

427
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,480
stores are licensed to sell tickets,

428
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:54,800
generate steady foot traffic from

429
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:56,520
regular players. And the station earns a

430
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:59,400
commission on every ticket sold,

431
00:14:56,520 --> 00:15:01,320
typically 5 to 6%. When a station sells

432
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:03,200
a winning ticket for a major jackpot,

433
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:05,160
the resulting local media attention

434
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:06,839
drives a documented spike in ticket

435
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:08,960
sales at that location for weeks

436
00:15:06,839 --> 00:15:10,560
afterward. Modern stations are also

437
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:13,080
adding electric vehicle charging

438
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:15,480
stations. A level two commercial charger

439
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:18,480
costs around $3,500

440
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:21,320
in hardware, plus another $2,500 for

441
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:23,400
installation. A DC fast charger, the

442
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:27,680
kind that can add significant range in

443
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:29,840
20 to 40 minutes, runs 35,000 to 140,000

444
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:32,080
dollars for the hardware alone, plus

445
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:34,080
another 20,000 to 80,000 for the

446
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:35,440
electrical infrastructure to support it.

447
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:37,720
The federal government's national

448
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:40,160
electric vehicle infrastructure program,

449
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:42,960
funded at 5 billion dollars, covers up

450
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:44,720
to 80% of eligible installation costs

451
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:47,040
for stations on designated highway

452
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:48,920
corridors, which has made the economics

453
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:50,840
considerably more attractive. And the

454
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:52,760
appeal for station operators is not just

455
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:55,040
the charging revenue, it is the dwell

456
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:57,080
time. A driver charging for 30 minutes

457
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:59,200
buys coffee, eats a sandwich, and

458
00:15:57,080 --> 00:16:01,080
browses the store. That is the longest,

459
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:03,160
most profitable customer visit a gas

460
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:05,160
station can capture. Revenue is not

461
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:07,040
profit, and in this business the gap

462
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:08,840
between those two numbers is enormous.

463
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:11,360
Labor is the biggest line item. A

464
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:13,800
24-hour station needs multiple employees

465
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:15,520
per shift, 7 days a week, 52 weeks a

466
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:17,480
year. The average convenience store

467
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:19,320
employs roughly 20 people, and the

468
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:21,480
industry average wage has been rising

469
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:24,040
steadily. Payroll, including all the

470
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:25,920
taxes, benefits, and overtime, is

471
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:28,200
typically the largest single operating

472
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:30,200
expense. Utilities are significant and

473
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:33,320
often overlooked. Those walk-in beer

474
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:35,160
coolers run continuously 24 hours a day.

475
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:37,160
The outdoor canopy lighting stays on all

476
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:39,240
night. The air conditioning in summer

477
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:40,960
and heat in winter for a 3,000 square

478
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:43,200
foot building with constantly opening

479
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:45,320
doors adds up fast. The average

480
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:47,920
convenience store pays around 23,000

481
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:50,160
dollars per year in electricity alone.

482
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:52,240
Credit card fees, as mentioned, are not

483
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:54,080
just a fuel problem. They apply to every

484
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:56,440
transaction in the store as well.

485
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:58,520
Equipment maintenance is relentless.

486
00:16:56,440 --> 00:17:00,640
Dispensers break. Underground sensors

487
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:02,480
need calibration. Cooler compressors

488
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:04,520
fail. Point of sale systems need

489
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:06,079
updates. The physical infrastructure of

490
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:08,439
a gas station is under constant

491
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:10,480
mechanical stress. Then there is theft.

492
00:17:08,439 --> 00:17:12,079
Drive-offs, where a driver fills up and

493
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:13,640
leaves without paying, still happen

494
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:16,120
despite prepay requirements in most

495
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:18,240
states. Internal theft from employees is

496
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:20,520
an ongoing challenge. Card skimming

497
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:22,199
devices, where criminals attach illegal

498
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:23,959
readers to fuel dispensers to steal

499
00:17:22,199 --> 00:17:25,600
customer card data, have cost the

500
00:17:23,959 --> 00:17:27,480
industry hundreds of millions of dollars

501
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:30,480
in fraud liability and equipment

502
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:32,440
replacement costs and insurance. A gas

503
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:34,640
station carries general liability,

504
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:36,640
property insurance, and something most

505
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:39,080
businesses never need to think about,

506
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:41,240
pollution liability insurance. Because

507
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:43,200
if something goes wrong underground, the

508
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:45,040
cleanup is your problem. This is the

509
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:47,120
part of the gas station business that

510
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:48,640
keeps owners up at night. Buried beneath

511
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:50,400
every gas station are steel or

512
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:52,960
fiberglass tanks holding thousands of

513
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:55,160
gallons of gasoline. The EPA requires

514
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:57,160
these tanks to be double walled, a tank

515
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:59,280
inside a tank with sensors in the space

516
00:17:57,160 --> 00:18:01,000
between the walls to detect any leakage.

517
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:03,120
They require automatic tank gauging

518
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,280
systems that continuously monitor fuel

519
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:07,000
levels for unexplained losses.

520
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:09,160
They require vapor recovery systems on

521
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,120
the dispensers to capture fumes. They

522
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:12,960
require statistical software that cross

523
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:15,440
references daily sales and delivery

524
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:17,520
volumes to flag any discrepancy that

525
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:19,600
might indicate a slow leak. All of that

526
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:21,520
compliance costs money. A basic leak

527
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:24,120
detection system for a standard three

528
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:26,840
tank station runs between $3,000 and

529
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:29,320
$8,000. Upgrading older tanks with

530
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:30,960
corrosion protection can cost $10,000 to

531
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:32,880
$48,000.

532
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:35,200
Installing new tanks from scratch runs

533
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:37,080
into the hundreds of thousands, but the

534
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:40,480
bigger risk is what happens if something

535
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:43,240
leaks anyway. As of March 2026, the EPA

536
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:44,680
has recorded over 583,000

537
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:46,800
confirmed releases from underground

538
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:49,680
storage tank systems across the United

539
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:51,960
States. More than 54,000 sites still

540
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:53,840
need cleanup. The average cleanup cost

541
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:57,560
per site is approximately is the

542
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:57,560
average. Contamination

543
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:01,160
that reaches the ground water, which is

544
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:03,480
the drinking water source for nearly

545
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:05,640
half of all Americans, can push that

546
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:07,760
number into the millions. Ground water

547
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:09,640
remediation requires drilling monitoring

548
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:11,400
wells, installing pump and treat

